From: Steffen Jaeckel <sjaeckel@suse.de>
Subject: kABI fix for new dropreasons
Patch-mainline: Never, kABI workaround
References: CVE-2026-53091 bsc#1269530 bsc#1273418

This is a combined kABI fix for multiple commits which add a new drop
reason and would therefore break kABI.

We remove the new element instead from the `#define DEFINE_DROP_REASON`
and set the value of the new enum element to
`SKB_DROP_REASON_NOT_SPECIFIED`, so we can keep the code as is.

Since the dropreason is only used for debugging purposes, this should
pose no risk.

This handles the addition of a new dropreason for the following
mainline commits:
* SKB_BAD_GSO from 7fb4c1967011 ("net: pull headers in
  qdisc_pkt_len_segs_init()")
* RECURSION_LIMIT from d15d3de94a47 ("net: Dropreason: add
  SKB_DROP_REASON_RECURSION_LIMIT")

Signed-off-by: Michal Kubecek <mkubecek@suse.cz>
Signed-off-by: Steffen Jaeckel <sjaeckel@suse.de>
Reviewed-by: Jan Kara <jack@suse.cz>
Reviewed-by: Michal Koutný <mkoutny@suse.com>
Acked-by: Michal Koutný <mkoutny@suse.com>
---
 include/net/dropreason-core.h | 19 +++++++++++++------
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

diff --git a/include/net/dropreason-core.h b/include/net/dropreason-core.h
index 41c9930e67ba..1c9f91cf69f3 100644
--- a/include/net/dropreason-core.h
+++ b/include/net/dropreason-core.h
@@ -64,7 +64,6 @@
 	FN(UNHANDLED_PROTO)		\
 	FN(SKB_CSUM)			\
 	FN(SKB_GSO_SEG)			\
-	FN(SKB_BAD_GSO)			\
 	FN(SKB_UCOPY_FAULT)		\
 	FN(DEV_HDR)			\
 	FN(DEV_READY)			\
@@ -93,7 +92,6 @@
 	FN(PACKET_SOCK_ERROR)		\
 	FN(TC_CHAIN_NOTFOUND)		\
 	FN(TC_RECLASSIFY_LOOP)		\
-	FN(RECURSION_LIMIT)		\
 	FNe(MAX)
 
 /**
@@ -316,8 +314,6 @@ enum skb_drop_reason {
 	SKB_DROP_REASON_SKB_CSUM,
 	/** @SKB_DROP_REASON_SKB_GSO_SEG: gso segmentation error */
 	SKB_DROP_REASON_SKB_GSO_SEG,
-	/** @SKB_DROP_REASON_SKB_BAD_GSO: malicious gso packet. */
-	SKB_DROP_REASON_SKB_BAD_GSO,
 	/**
 	 * @SKB_DROP_REASON_SKB_UCOPY_FAULT: failed to copy data from user space,
 	 * e.g., via zerocopy_sg_from_iter() or skb_orphan_frags_rx()
@@ -422,14 +418,25 @@ enum skb_drop_reason {
 	 * iterations.
 	 */
 	SKB_DROP_REASON_TC_RECLASSIFY_LOOP,
-	/** @SKB_DROP_REASON_RECURSION_LIMIT: Dead loop on virtual device. */
-	SKB_DROP_REASON_RECURSION_LIMIT,
 	/**
 	 * @SKB_DROP_REASON_MAX: the maximum of core drop reasons, which
 	 * shouldn't be used as a real 'reason' - only for tracing code gen
 	 */
 	SKB_DROP_REASON_MAX,
 
+#ifndef __GENKSYMS__
+        /**
+	 * In order to prevent kABI breakage, but keeping the sources as is,
+	 * keep the newly introduced enum entries, but define them to an
+	 * existing value.
+	 */
+
+        /** @SKB_DROP_REASON_SKB_BAD_GSO: malicious gso packet. */
+        SKB_DROP_REASON_SKB_BAD_GSO = SKB_DROP_REASON_NOT_SPECIFIED,
+        /** @SKB_DROP_REASON_RECURSION_LIMIT: Dead loop on virtual device. */
+        SKB_DROP_REASON_RECURSION_LIMIT = SKB_DROP_REASON_NOT_SPECIFIED,
+#endif
+
 	/**
 	 * @SKB_DROP_REASON_SUBSYS_MASK: subsystem mask in drop reasons,
 	 * see &enum skb_drop_reason_subsys
-- 
